; appended to S:User-Startup by the installer
; The boot-time Assign is what makes the interpreter find its stdlib (/Python).
; The launcher itself is installed to C: (always on the path) so that typing
; `python` works from any Shell, including Wanderer's NewShell, after a reboot -
; `Path Python:S ADD` here would only affect the boot shell, not a NewShell.
Assign Python: SYS:Python
